Ev gund e, giş wêde bibî.
 
This is the village, all of it is over there.

134
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Emê noka bisewirînin.
 
We will film it now.

135
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Aaah...
 
Aaah...

136
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Maşallah, erê gundekî biçûk e bes xweş e.
 
Mashallah, yes it is a small village but it is pleasant.

137
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Rêya xwe, rêya reîsî zift e.
 
Its road, the main road is asphalt.

138
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Taben, ev mefreqa hember me...
 
Of course, this intersection opposite us...

139
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Ev mefreqa hember me, cem wî sîndiyana ra, diçe Şera.
 
This intersection opposite us, by that oak tree, goes to
Sharran.

140
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Ew rêka diçe Şera.
 
That road goes to Sharran.

141
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Şera, bêbê nêzîk e. Sê çar kîlo ne.
 
Sharran, man, is close. It's three or four kilometers.

142
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Hevalno vî derê jî em li gundê Gobelaka, li mala Ebû Xelîl
rûniştî bûn.
 
Friends, here too we were sitting in Gobelaka village, at
Abu Khalil's house.

143
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Me go wele, me teswîr kir, îlla hilebîlî, were em qehweke
vexwin.
 
We said, by God, we filmed, absolutely, come let's drink a
coffee.

144
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Taben Ebû Xelîl jî ne xerîb e.
 
Of course, Abu Khalil is not a stranger either.

145
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Mehra xwe li Behdîna jî, li Memala jî anîye.
 
He brought his dowry (wife) from Bahdina, and from Mamala
too.

146
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Emê nîvandir bin.
 
We will be in between.

147
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Ser serî me. Xalo, ev der mala kê ye?
 
You're welcome. Uncle, whose house is this?

148
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Bi rastî bêjim, Gobelaka mala Reşîd Heskotîkê ye. Ev mala
Heskotîkê ye, vî derê jî Gobelaka ye.
 
To tell the truth, in Gobelaka this is Rashid Heskotik's
house. This is Heskotik's house, and this place is Gobelaka.

149
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Taben Gobelaka jî giş yek bavik in. Kesî xerîb tê tune, hewa
mala apê min e, hewa mala pismamê min e, kesî xerîb tê tune.
 
Of course, Gobelaka are all one lineage. There are no
strangers in it, that is my uncle's house, that is my
cousin's house, there are no strangers.

150
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Em giş, ji yek bavikî ne. Ê me kesî xerîb tê tune ne.
 
We are all from one father. We have no strangers among us.

151
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Ne wekî dibên giş, em xal û xwarzi ne.
 
Not like they say, everyone, we are maternal uncles and
nephews.

152
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Xwedê ji te razî be. Nono, maşallah min dî seqfê gunda giş
bi hev ve ne, min tewlê mego, ano gerek giş meyrî hev bin.
 
May God be pleased with you. No no, Mashallah I saw the
roofs of the village are all connected, I told them, they
must all be loving to each other.

153
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Xûlû meyrî ta Behdîna pirr in.
 
Man, the love/ties to Bahdina are many.

154
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Behdîna hene maşallah, Behdîna me em xarzê Memala ne, xarzê
mala Ehmedê Xelîl in em.
 
Bahdina is there Mashallah, our Bahdina, we are nephews of
Mamala, we are nephews of Ahmed Khalil's family.

155
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Dikin dixwazin, me'kî dibên dost û ehbabê me jî lê hene,
meyrê me jî lê hene.
 
They visit and want, as they say our friends and loved ones
are there too, our affections are there too.

156
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Behdîna jî hene.
 
Bahdina is there too.

157
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Û ehlen û sehlen ji we ra, xêr jî hatin vê qenalê we.
 
And welcome to you, welcome to this channel of yours.

158
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Ser serî me û ser çavê me.
 
On our heads and on our eyes (You are very welcome).

159
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Saet xweş, Xwedê ji te razî be. Xalo, qîzika te li Ewropa
tûne?
 
Good times (Thank you), may God be pleased with you. Uncle,
don't you have a daughter in Europe?

160
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Na, evê Xwedê we bide lê, qîzika min tûne ne.
 
No, may God give you one, but I don't have daughters
[there].

161
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Xwedê we bide, lawê min hene.
 
May God give you, I have sons.

162
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Lawê min li Hecî Îsanî me nas dike, li ser vê qenalê...
 
My son knows Hajj Isani, on this channel...

163
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Ma'rûfim wekî dibên ez Hec Reşîd im ji Gobelaka, pişqê apê
min jî li derve hene.
 
I am known, as they say, I am Hajj Rashid from Gobelaka, my
uncle's children are also outside (abroad).

164
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Heye însanekî Kurmanc ji Efrînê giş 366 gunda, silavê min ji
şababê Ewropa gişî ra hene.
 
Every Kurmanji person from Afrin, all 366 villages, my
greetings go to all the youth in Europe.

165
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Ji gişî ra.
 
To all of them.

166
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Û ji vê qenalê ra jî, xûdêrim Mihemed ra heye ji Behdîna
kekê Mihemed.
 
And to this channel too, specifically to Mohammed from
Bahdina, brother Mohammed.

167
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Ji qenalê gund ra, û ehlen û sehlen ji we ra.
 
To the village channel, and welcome to you.

168
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Saet xweş, Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike.
 
Thank you, may God prolong your life.

169
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:35,000
De hede, Xwedê bedana we şên bike, Xwedê we nake bêpar da.
 
Come on then, may God make your bodies prosperous, may God
not leave you deprived.

170
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Her yekî li vê vîdyû sêr dike, miletê gundê Gobelaka, biçûk
mezin, silavê min ji were hene, çavê giya maç dikim, Xwedê
ji we razî be.
 
Everyone watching this video, people of Gobelaka village,
small and big, my greetings to you, I kiss everyone's eyes,
may God be pleased with you.

171
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Emê noho lextaneke xweş nav gundê we jî werin teswîr kin, û
vîdyo jî belav kin, bişînin ji hevdû ra, bila lê sêr kin,
newî?
 
We will now film a nice clip inside your village, and share
the video, send it to each other, let them watch it, right?

172
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Ehlen û sehlen, şababê Ewropa giş ra, Kurmancê giş ra.
 
Welcome, to all the youth of Europe, to all Kurmanjis.

173
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Car perça Kurdistanê ra.
 
To the four parts of Kurdistan.

174
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Erê, Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Yes, may God be pleased with you.

175
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Sarinca, tewr û kevir, di Gobelaka da heye. Heye sarinca bî.
 
The cistern, the pick and stone, is in Gobelaka. There is an
[old] cistern.

176
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Kevnar heye û...
 
It is ancient and...

177
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Vê dîwarê dibêjin, yimkin emrê gundê ser 700 salî ra ye.
 
They call this wall... maybe the age of the village is over
700 years.

178
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Xûlû vê sahê çi kar dikirin têda?
 
Man, what work did they do in this square?

179
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Vê sahê berê bêderdî didan, kûlket me bêderdî didan viderê,
haşo berê bi qatira bû, bi dera bû.
 
In this square before they used to dump rubbish, we dumped
rubbish here, sorry, before it was with mules, with donkeys.

180
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Giş bêderdî didan viderê, bêderê xwe li viderê kom dikirin.
 
Everyone dumped rubbish here, they gathered their thrashing
floor here.

181
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Şînî guncî dihat av ji viderê jî dibir.
 
Green vegetables came, they took water from here too.

182
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Maşallah, maşallah.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

183
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Erê, û ji viderê dibên kaniya av dihat viderê.
 
Yes, and from here they say the spring water came here.

184
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Berê heye hinekî... viderê makinê danî tê.
 
Before there was some... here they put a machine in it.

185
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Donote?
 
Donote (Engine brand)?

186
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Donote.
 
Donote.

187
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Heye rêk heye, em berê gund ra hono derê, hemberî vî go darê
reş, darê zeytûna heye ji darê reş.
 
There is a road, we go in front of the village like this,
opposite this where the black tree is, there are olive trees
from the black tree [type].

188
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Te berê avê kişandî serî çi, jiber met'emê Mihemed?
 
Did you pull water before on top of what, because of
Mohammed's restaurant?

189
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Na. Xweş e ava viderê pir xweş e.
 
No. It's good, the water here is very good.

190
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Avê vî, ava cama do pirr ne.
 
This water, the water of the community is plentiful.

191
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Bîrê avê ji nîvê gund û jêr da hene?
 
Are there water wells from the middle of the village
downwards?

192
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Ewa. Giş heşk bûn.
 
Yes. They all dried up.

193
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Giş heşk bûn.
 
They dried up?

194
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Giş heşk bûn.
 
They all dried up.

195
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Erê, giş heşk bûn.
 
Was it a drought?

196
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Erê, giş heşk bûn.
 
Yes, they all dried up.

197
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Maşallah hevalno, wadî ye, gundekî pirr xweş û kîbar e.
 
Mashallah friends, as you can see, it is a very nice and
elegant village.

198
00:16:54,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Noka hîn ezê tiştê xweş wara darxem.
 
Now I will still show you nice things.

199
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Go ev mala...
 
He said this is the house of...

200
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Mala Zekeriya.
 
Zekeriya's house.

201
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Gobelaka xuyanî ne xweş e.
 
Gobelaka is visible, it's nice.

202
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Yanî heşîniyê xwe, dar û berê xwe heye, bes hewa heta şarê
rêk nîne.
 
Meaning it has its greenery, its trees and fruits, but that
road until the main road doesn't exist.

203
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Na şarê rêk tûne. Têkev dît, em kanîn vira têkevin, makîne
sayare.
 
Where is the road?

204
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Na şarê rêk tûne. Têkev dît, em kanîn vira têkevin, makîne
sayare.
 
No, there is no main road. You saw entering, we can enter
here, machines and cars.

205
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Ewa...
 
Yeah...

206
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Maşallah hevalno we dîye? Gundekî pirr xweş û kîbar e.
 
Mashallah friends, did you see? A very nice and elegant
village.

207
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Av noka qezîfa lê ketin, av noka xera bûn.
 
Now shells hit the water [infrastructure], the water is now
ruined.

208
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Rêk tûne heye ji derbasbûnê.
 
There is no road for passing.

209
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Heta jor naberin xûlû?
 
Do they not take it up to the top, man?

210
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Mixtêr gelek kir, mixtêr gelek kir, heva ziftê ji mera anîn
hatin, minezeme jî elesas heta çortê gund bibrin.
 
The mukhtar did a lot, the mukhtar did a lot, they brought
this asphalt for us, the organization also basically was
supposed to take it to the village intersection.

211
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Ê saetê mixtêr xweş, Xwedê jê razî be.
 
Well, bless the mukhtar's time, may God be pleased with him.

212
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Saetê gundê xweş.
 
Bless the village's time.

213
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Erê, mixtêr ewqir cihet kir, îda elesas wa danî mixtêr heta
mefreqa gund hanî.
 
Yes, the mukhtar made so much effort, so basically he placed
it, the mukhtar brought it up to the village intersection.

214
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Em dibêjin kî divê rêker û çûn, terabî ye.
 
We say whoever wants the road and going, it is dirt.

215
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Erê terabî ye.
 
Yes, it is dirt.

216
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Mihemed noka emê têkeve ber têkefinê.
 
Mohammed, now we will enter the entrance.

217
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Temam.
 
Okay.

218
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Cemaet hûretê we domayî, emê poşêr aharin wira. Yanî hema
hema derkê cem şebabê jî.
 
Folks, your small change is finished, we will put the cover
there. Meaning almost getting out to the guys too.

219
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Teberrû' da mektebê, bes bigû bila qîçik bixwînin.
 
He donated to the school, just saying let the kids study.

220
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Maşallah, Xwedê jê razî be.
 
Mashallah, may God be pleased with him.

221
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Vê zemanî da...
 
In this time...

222
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Û salî çûyî dîsa...
 
And last year again...

223
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Salî çûyî ş dûra dîsa 300, 200 û 40 kîlo met da ye.
 
Last year from afar he again gave 300, 240 kilo meters
(likely square meters of land).

224
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Go kîjan zêde bike, dîsa me dayê.
 
He said whoever adds more, we gave it again.

225
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Bê beramber.
 
Without return (for free).

226
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Xwedê jê razî be, Xwedê emrê kî dirêj bide.
 
May God be pleased with him, may God give him a long life.

227
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Min şûna mektebê min tebere' da mektebê, min go bila qîçikê
me xwendewan derkevin.
 
I donated the place for the school, I donated to the school,
I said let our children come out educated.

228
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Saet xweş, Xwedê jê razî be.
 
Bless you, may God be pleased with him.

229
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Û kê pirs dikim bila pirs ke.
 
And whoever asks, let them ask.

230
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Saetê wa xweş. Bixwînin ha!
 
Bless your time. Study, okay!

231
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Îşo ter derkevî ezê hediyo pê dimê.
 
Tonight if you go out, I will give you a gift.

232
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Hevalno li vê derê jî em li hewşa gundê Gobelaka ne.
 
Friends, here too we are in the courtyard of Gobelaka
village.

233
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Taben cisrê meydankê li kû, hember min e xuyan têt.
 
Of course, where is the Maydanki bridge, opposite me, it is
visible.

234
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Helûbiyê jî li wira.
 
Halubiya is there too.

235
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Da şarê jî li ko li hember min e. Em li hewşa gundin e, cem
xezonê avê.
 
The town is also opposite me. We are in the village
courtyard, by the water tank.

236
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Li vê derê jî hevalno...
 
Here too friends...

237
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Taben...
 
Of course...

238
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Ezê du gotina bikim li vê derê.
 
I will say two words here.

239
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Vê derê cemaat, bîreke avê heye, bîr caîz e.
 
Here folks, there is a water well, the well is ready.

240
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Vê derê.
 
This place.

241
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Xalû min ra dibê.
 
My uncle tells me.

242
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Hev avê jî, vê bîrê jî dex vî gundî dikir. Miletî vî gundî
pê vedixwar, pê sebeb dibî.
 
This water too, this well too, used to pump to this village.
The people of this village drank from it, it was a source
(of life).

243
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Li vê derê bîr heye, xetasî gundî tê werbîye.
 
There is a well here, the village submersible pump has
fallen into it.

244
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
Bîr heye, xetasî gundî tê werbîye.
 
The well is there, the village pump has fallen in.

245
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Û elwah şemsîyê dixwaze.
 
And it requires solar panels.

246
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Alwah şemsîye û xetasî gundî, saglem derxin.
 
Solar panels and the village pump, if they get it out
intact.

247
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Alwah şemsîye bi rakbînin.
 
If they install solar panels.

248
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Vê milletî vî gundî giş dike ava vexwe.
 
All the people of this village will drink water.

249
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Xalû ji dibê kes tûne mara av bike.
 
My uncle also says there is no one to provide water for us.

250
00:19:55,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Ez temenna, ez temenna, teben em sebîlata çêdikin ji milet
ra. No xokek min...
 
I hope, I hope, of course we build fountains (charity water)
for the people. Now a peach of mine...

251
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Ji gundî Me'melo, me ra teberu' kir, saeta gundê xweş...
 
From the village of Ma'amelo, a donation was made to us,
bless the village...

252
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Xokê min navî gundê Henîn e...
 
My uncle, the name of the village is Henîn [referring to the
man or location]...

253
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Ji gundî Me'melo ye, me ra teberu' kir, em kê sebîlekê li
gundê Me'melo çêkin.
 
He is from the village of Ma'amelo, he donated to us, so we
can build a public fountain in the village of Ma'amelo.

254
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Sebîl jî na, serinc e.
 
Not just a fountain, it's a cistern.

255
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Ê gundê Ba'dîno me serinc çêkir, ji xaltîka Olmaz ra.
 
For the village of Ba'dino, we built a cistern, from Auntie
Olmaz.

256
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Me teberu' kir ji milet ra.
 
We donated it for the people.

257
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Û xokê min Me'melo jî Henîn, wî jî teberu' kir...
 
And my uncle from Ma'amelo, Henîn, he also donated...

258
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Em kê bîrek a ê li mileta gundê Me'melo ra em kê bikulin.
 
We will dig a water well for the people of Ma'amelo village.

259
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Me'nî mileta gundê Me'melo a ê vexwe, gundî 'emmar e...
 
Meaning the people of Ma'amelo village will drink, the
village is prosperous...

260
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Me ro vê avê ne, ro jê vederê tên cem a Ba'dîno dibin.
 
As for this water, the road is from here until it reaches
Ba'dino.

261
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Ko wer hevalê min.
 
Come here, my friend.

262
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Miletî, miletî gundê Me'melo û 'emmarê ra tên Ba'dîno avê
dibin.
 
The people, the people of Ma'amelo and 'Emmar villages take
water to Ba'dino.

263
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Her neqlekê tên ji vê avê ji cem a Ba'dîno dibin, tizanî
teklîfî xwe jî pir e.
 
Every trip they take from this water to Ba'dino, you know
the cost is high.

264
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Yanî neqlê bi bîst dolaran, bîst û pênc dolaran, ê mezin jî
bi pêncî dolarî digihînin wura.
 
Meaning a trip is twenty dollars, twenty-five dollars, and
the large ones reach fifty dollars to get there.

265
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Hecî jî cafav be, ê milet pir êşek dî, milet yanî...
 
Since it is a drought, the people have suffered a lot, the
people mean...

266
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Pir êqintî bî me'nî avê.
 
There was a lot of distress regarding water.

267
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Ê emê hefarekê wur lêxin, bîrê avê.
 
So we will set up a drilling rig there, a water well.

268
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Me'nî vê miletê girtî avê vexwe.
 
Meaning all these people will drink water.

269
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Sebîlillah, xêrî u çin.
 
For the sake of God, charity and such.

270
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Yekî ji bû rihî dê kî xwe çêke, me ro xaltîka teberu' kirî,
çavê gindê maç dikim.
 
Someone might build it for the soul of their mother, just as
the Auntie donated to us, I kiss her eyes [thank her
deeply].

271
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,000
We etemene jî...
 
And I hope also...

272
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Wek xaltîka Olmaz, wek xokê me Henîn, xêrxwaz li dinyayê pir
bibin.
 
Like Auntie Olmaz, like our Uncle Henîn, may charitable
people increase in the world.

273
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Em mantiqa xwe şên bikin, her însan ne bi rengekî xizmet
dike.
 
So we can revitalize our region, every human serves in a
different way.

274
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Hinek teberu'ata çê dikin ji feqîr û sewîyora, saeta giya
xweş.
 
Some make donations for the poor and orphans, bless them
all.

275
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Hinek bîrê avê dikulin, hinek hêşînayê diçînin.
 
Some dig water wells, some plant greenery.

276
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Saeta giya xweş, iştam key mantiqa xwe şên kin, em kê rind
kin, tiştê rind darxîn.
 
Bless them all, as long as we revitalize our region, make it
good, and produce good things.

277
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,000
Erê hevalno, bîyê avê jî heva ye.
 
Yes friends, the water well is this one.

278
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Wer hevalê min nîzik bike.
 
Come here my friend, get closer.

279
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Xalo, heva çiqas kûr e?
 
Uncle, how deep is this?

280
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Xwedê heva bi xwe sê sed û sê mître ye.
 
By God, this itself is three hundred and three meters.

281
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Sê sed û sê mître? No xatas têdaye? Berim camê de were.
 
Three hundred and three meters? Is the submersible pump
inside? Turn the glass [camera] here.

282
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Xatas neha têdaye, heva bi xwe sê sed û sê mître ye.
 
The submersible pump is not in it yet, this itself is three
hundred and three meters deep.

283
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
Heva amade bi xwe wekî dibên, am bi xwe hazir bûye.
 
This is ready itself as they say, we are ready.

284
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Heva sê sed û sê mître... kî...
 
This is three hundred and three meters... that...

285
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,000
Avê xwe rind e?
 
Is its water good?

286
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Avê xwe rind e.
 
Its water is good.

287
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Zêdayî wekî dibên deh gund têkir, û zêde jî dimîne.
 
It's enough to satisfy ten villages as they say, and there
will be extra left over.

288
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
Zêde jî dimîne, lê çi tişt jê kêm e neha?
 
There will be extra, but what is missing from it now?

289
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Tiştê kêm, xatasek jê ra lazim e bi xartûmê gindê va, û lewh
şemsiye, û cîhazê gendalê bikevin.
 
The missing things, a submersible pump is needed with pipes
going up, and solar panels, and the inverter device to go
in.

290
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,000
Ev tişto garakê me ye.
 
These are the things we need.

291
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,000
Û lûlabê xwe derê xwe caiz e ne?
 
And its taps and its place are ready, right?

292
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:15,000
Caiz e, caiz e, xezanê xwe jî caiz e, bes av ji viderê
derkeve xezên, tewzî' mal bi mal dibe.
 
Ready, ready, its tank is also ready, just water needs to
come out from here to the tank, distribution happens house
by house.

293
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Teba'an heva av ji vir derkeve, weyî çûçik binî ma xezan e.
 
Naturally, this water comes out from here, that small one
below us is the tank.

294
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,000
Xezan e.
 
It is a tank.

295
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Ê ji vir derkeve xezanê...
 
So it comes out from here to the tank...

296
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Xezanê tije bibe, paşê henefî lûla vedikin...
 
The tank fills up, then they open the taps...

297
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:24,000
Bela dikin derê gund giş.
 
They distribute it to the whole village.

298
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Tewzî' giş dibe?
 
It distributes to everyone?

299
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:29,000
Bûy, heta vê hemberê, vê hemberê malek vê avê namîne giş
vedixwin.
 
Yes, even to the opposite side, not a single house on the
opposite side will be left without water, they will all
drink.

300
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:34,000
Are saeta we xweş, em dixwazin bi me ra yardim bikin vê
avê...
 
Yes, bless you, we want you to help us with this water...

301
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Me'nî bi me ra, em dixwazin hawara bikin.
 
Meaning for us, we want to make a plea.

302
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Înşallah, kesê xêrxwaz hebin, wek xaltîka Olmaz û wek xokê
me Henîn...
 
God willing, if there are charitable people, like Auntie
Olmaz and like our Uncle Henîn...

303
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:44,000
Kelak me bigirin, teba'an miletî me jî pir li Ewropayê ye.
 
Support us, naturally many of our people are in Europe.

304
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:47,000
Em qane fedakî ji wa bibînin, çavê giya maç dikim.
 
We hope to see some sacrifice from them, I kiss all their
eyes.

305
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:52,000
Û rehma li mirîyê wa giya bin, ber destê mirîyê wa giya bin,
Xwedê rizqê wa bide şînê.
 
And mercy be upon all their dead, before the hands of all
their dead, may God increase their livelihood.

306
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:59,000
Yanî îşta ji wî, ji wî, ji wî, ji wî, em ê vê bîrê
bişixulînin û milet jî vexwê kêf xweş bibe.
 
Meaning now from this one, from that one, from this one,
from that one, we will operate this well and the people will
drink and be happy.

307
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Û ê pir du'a li wa bikin, heva jî tê hesibandin wek
sebîlekî.
 
And they will pray for them a lot, this is also considered
like a public charity (sabil).

308
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Sedeqe cariye çi dibe av e.
 
An ongoing charity, what is it? It is water.

309
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Erê, ê hev 'idda garakê xwe ye, xatas e û lewh şemsîyene
garakê xwe ye.
 
Yes, so this equipment is needed, a submersible pump and
solar panels are needed.

310
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Û teba'an hefare jî amê wînin, me'nî vê xatasî tê werbî ji
me ra jê bikşîne.
 
And naturally we will bring the drilling rig, meaning to put
this submersible pump in so it pulls [water] for us.

311
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Jê derxe.
 
Extract it.

312
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Bi pûlê te jê derdixin.
 
They extract it with your money.

313
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Û inşallah kesê xêrxwaz hebe kelak me bigire, xalo.
 
And God willing, if there is a charitable person, they will
support us, Uncle.

314
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Saeta we xweş û ji qenalê we ra, Hecî Îsongî Kurmanc ji
her...
 
Bless you and your channel, Hecî Îsongî Kurmanc from
every...

315
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Îsanekî Kurmanc ji mantiqê Efrîn û wele xêr...
 
Every Kurdish person from the Afrin region and elsewhere...

316
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Silavê me ji giya ra hene.
 
Our greetings to all of them.

317
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Û in heta em kanebin vê avê bi vî miletî ra hawara bikin.
 
And so that we can help these people with this water.

318
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Îsan heye neqlê avê bi pênc sed wereq dikiire.
 
There are people buying a water tanker trip for five hundred
notes [currency].

319
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Gucî xu nagihînî.
 
They cannot afford it.

320
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Nagihînê, hefteyêkê pênc darr...
 
They can't afford it, five times a week...

321
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Şuxul tune, ma'aşek tune, tiştek tune.
 
There is no work, no salary, nothing.

322
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:44,000
Ê heye dor û vê av dimîne.
 
Those who exist are left waiting for a turn for this water.

323
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:44,000
Em ji wa dixwazin, hecî însankî Kurmanc li derveyî welat li
ku dibe.
 
That's right.

324
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Em ji wa dixwazin, hecî însankî Kurmanc li derveyî welat li
ku dibe.
 
We ask of them, every Kurdish person outside the country
wherever they are.

325
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Ne em kê bêjin wele hane, em dixwazin ji gund giya ra ye.
 
Not that we say look here, we want it for the whole village.

326
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Erê icbûrî ye teba'an hevalo em îcbur nakin kesî.
 
Yes, it is voluntary naturally friends, we don't force
anyone.

327
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:58,000
Em dibên kesê xêrxwaz, kesê daxwazê teberu'ekî çêke...
 
We say a charitable person, a person who wishes to make a
donation...

328
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Ji milet ra em vê bîrê temam bikin, avê gundê derxin.
 
For the people, so we can finish this well, extract the
village's water.

329
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Teba'an caiz e, bes xatas têda mekinî ye.
 
Naturally it is ready, only the submersible pump is not
inside.

330
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:09,000
Û lewh şemsiye, em avê dax gund kin, mla gund fêdê bibîne.
 
And solar panels, so we can pump water to the village, so
the village sees the benefit.

331
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:11,000
Û ê pir du'a ji we ra bikin.
 
And they will pray for you a lot.

332
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Heva jî tê hasibandin wek sebîlekî.
 
This is also considered like a public charity.

333
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:15,000
Sedeqe cariye çi dibe av e.
 
An ongoing charity, what is it? It is water.

334
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

335
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Ê hav 'idda garakê xwe ye, xatas û lewh şemsîye ne, garakê
xwe ye.
 
So this equipment is needed, the submersible pump and solar
panels are needed.

336
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:24,000
Û teba'an hefare jî amê wînin, me'nî vê xatasî tê werbî ji
me ra jê bikşîne.
 
And naturally we will bring the drilling rig, meaning to put
this submersible pump in so it pulls [water] for us.

337
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Jê derxe.
 
Extract it.

338
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,000
Bi pûlê te jê derdixin.
 
They extract it with money.

339
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Û inşallah kesê xêrxwaz hebe kelak me bigire, xalo.
 
And God willing, if there is a charitable person, they will
support us, Uncle.

340
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,000
Ka wer darbas be xalo darbas be.
 
Come here, pass by uncle, pass by.

341
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:33,000
Yalla.
 
Let's go.

342
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:37,000
Heva jî hewzê avê, av ji bîrê derê dihot vê hewzoyî.
 
This is also the water tank, water comes from the well into
this tank.

343
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Heva tije dibe.
 
This fills up.

344
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Tije dibe, û dax gund dike, mal bi mal, giştek av, darê
gî... gund...
 
It fills up, and pumps to the village, house by house, all
water, to the whole... village...

345
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Mal bi mal.
 
House by house.

346
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Gî vedixwin?
 
Everyone drinks?

347
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Giş vedixwin.
 
Everyone drinks.

348
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Ê wano be avê wekî mistemir hebe.
 
So it shouldn't be that the water is continuous [implying
current lack].

349
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Mistemir heye, maşallah av bîro jî nacih e, sê sed û sê
mître ye.
 
It is continuous [potentially], mashallah the well water is
successful too, it is three hundred and three meters.

350
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

351
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:57,000
Wano be avê henefî ye mistemir ê hebe.
 
It shouldn't be that tap water is continuous [now].

352
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Hecdeh salê gûnî nîzamê da, av zêde dibî, av bi hespîn ma
fêdê nedikirist bîr.
 
For eighteen years under the old regime, there was excess
water, we thought water was plentiful so we didn't worry
about the well.

353
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:05,000
Gi tîr av dibûn.
 
Everyone was satiated with water.

354
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:07,000
Nokre em dibersin têra ro nagihîne.
 
Now we fear it won't be enough.

355
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:12,000
Sîter pênc sed wereq, şeş sed wereq, da pênc bermîl av ji
mer otîni tî.
 
A tanker is five hundred notes, six hundred notes, to bring
us five barrels of water.

356
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:14,000
Û hefte yekê tê bikirî.
 
And you have to buy it once a week.

357
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Noker ma çend bîr lêxistin nav gundo jî av hişk bû.
 
Now we dug several wells in the village but the water went
dry.

358
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Hişk bû, tine, cefaf e.
 
It went dry, there isn't any, it's a drought.

359
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,000
Cefaf, cefaf e, nokra av tine ye.
 
Drought, it is a drought, now there is no water.

360
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Nokra em derin ji gundot avê da digirin tînin tê neqlê bi
pênc sed wereq tînin tê da pênc bermîl av.
 
Now we go to the villages to get water, we bring a trip for
five hundred notes to bring five barrels of water.

361
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Cem'a jî.
 
The community too.

362
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,000
Cem'a jî heye, milet heye nikane avê bikire.
 
The community is there too, there are people who cannot buy
water.

363
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Erê hevalno, teba'an...
 
Yes friends, naturally...

364
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Bi navî min, Efrîn sê-sê-şeş-şeş, Ebû Azad.
 
In my name, Afrin 3366, Abu Azad.

365
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Bi navî xolû...
 
In the name of Uncle...

366
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:39,000
Hecî Îsokî Kurd.
 
Hecî Îsokî the Kurd.

367
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:41,000
Em dengî xwe digihînin miletî ma yê Kurd...
 
We send our voice to our Kurdish people...

368
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:43,000
Li çi dûr dibe, çi nîzik dibe.
 
Wherever they are far, or near.

369
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:47,000
Kesê kanê bi me ra teberu' kê, em sebîlke li viderê çêkin.
 
Anyone who can donate to us, so we can build a public
fountain here.

370
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Wekî dibê spasî ya, wa spas dikim, ma çavê wa giya maç
dikim.
 
As they say thank you, I thank them, I kiss all their eyes.

371
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Ev jî xêr e, ev jî wekî dibê, sebîl carîye çi wer dibên.
 
This is also charity, this is as they say, an ongoing
charity as it is called.

372
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:57,000
Erê, sedeqe carîye.
 
Yes, ongoing charity.

373
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,000
Sedeqe carîye, viderê.
 
Ongoing charity, right here.

374
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:03,000
Û inşallah em ê wecbê xwe jî rabin, me berê didu çêkirin, du
sebîl me çêkirin.
 
And God willing we will fulfill our duty, we built two
before, we built two public fountains.

375
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Û inşallah em ê vê jî temam bikin, xêrxwaz pir in ji dinyayê
da.
 
And God willing we will finish this one too, there are many
charitable people in the world.

376
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,000
Saeta we xweş.
 
Bless you.

377
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Hecî însankî harikê, saeta giya de xweş, û wî harî neke jî
saeta wî ya giya xweş.
 
Every person who helps, bless them all, and those who don't
help, bless them all too.

378
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Û Xwedê wa bêle, û em dixwazin em dengê xwe wa jî bibîsin, û
vê qenalê ra em pir şa bûne, kêfxweş.
 
And may God leave them [protect them], and we want our voice
to be heard by them, and we are very happy with this
channel, joyful.

379
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:23,000
Ji qenalê Kekî Mihemed re hûr, otî gundî Gobelekê ra...
 
For the channel of Brother Mihemed, coming to the village of
Gobelek...

380
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,000
Em pir kêfxweş bûn e.
 
We were very happy.

381
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Saeta te xweş xolo, teba'an...
 
Bless you uncle, naturally...

382
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:29,000
Em te dêbîsin qenalê te û derê te ra.
 
We hear you, regarding your channel and your place.

383
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:35,000
Û em pir ji te hez dikin jî, û şe'bê me Kurmanc a gi, li
kêlek Kekî Mihemed bisekinin, mutabe'a bikin.
 
And we love you very much too, and all our Kurdish people,
stand beside Brother Mihemed, follow him.

384
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

385
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:40,000
Teba'an em tiştê xirab nakin, ma tiştê xirab kir, xeyrê
kûglî li me sêr me kin.
 
Naturally we don't do bad things, if we did bad things, then
don't watch us.

386
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Em dogazin em mantiqa xwe şên bikin.
 
We ask to revitalize our region.

387
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Bi çi dibe, mila bibe, em xizmetkî bikin ji miletê xwe ra,
em pêş kevin lo.
 
Whatever it takes, let it be, let us do a service for our
people, let us move forward.

388
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Em pêş kevin, na way xolo?
 
Let us move forward, isn't that right uncle?

389
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:52,000
Çi bi feqîrokî ra be, çi sebîlek be, çi dorçandinek be.
 
Whether for a poor person, or a public fountain, or planting
trees.

390
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:57,000
Hûrû em kêfxweş dibin, yek darên gundo debên hûrû qicikê opî
me...
 
Then we will be happy, someone comes to the villages and
says look, our small...

391
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Ji Ewropa pere şandin, em kêfxweş dibin hûrû em daren
sarincekê kulane.
 
They sent money from Europe, we are happy when we go and dig
a cistern.

392
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:07,000
Dibê filanî şandî, em kêfxweş dibin. Em dixwazin mantiqê
Efrîn, ji vê xweştir jî bibe, ji vê kêftir jî bibe.
 
They say so-and-so sent it, we are happy. We want the Afrin
region to be better than this, happier than this.

393
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:10,000
İnşallah, inşallah, hîne xweş bibe inşallah.
 
God willing, God willing, may it become even better, God
willing.

394
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:13,000
